  "explanation": "Rewrite numerator:<br /><br />$3x+1 = \\frac{3}{2}(2x+1) - \\frac12$.<br /><br />Thus the integral splits into two parts.<br /><br />First part gives $\\frac{3}{2}\\ln|x^2+x+1|$.<br /><br />Second part uses completing square:<br /><br />$x^2+x+1 = (x+1/2)^2 + 3/4$.<br /><br />Thus result becomes $\\frac{3}{2}\\ln|x^2+x+1| - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\tan^{-1}(\\frac{2x+1}{\\sqrt3}) + C$.",
